                      "source": "Purdue OWL",
                      "resourceType": "Guide"
                    }
                  ],
                  "publication_status": "published",
                  "completion_criteria": "Study the core frameworks in \"Beyond Summary: Making an Arguable Claim\", verify the inline knowledge check, and apply the practical checklist."
                },
                {
                  "id": "05d7ff10-ad53-7364-37f8-56a4ab26d752",
                  "title": "Structured Abstracts & Roadmapping",
                  "blocks": [
                    {
                      "text": "IMRaD & Funnel Introductions",
                      "type": "heading",
                      "level": 2
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Effective scholarly introductions funnel smoothly from established domain consensus -> specific unresolved gap/tension (\"However, few studies examine...\") -> exact research objective and thesis. Concise signposting sentences save readers from losing track across dense 15-page papers.",
                      "type": "paragraph"
                    },
                    {
                      "term": "Research Gap Move",
                      "text": "Explicitly articulating what prior scholarship established and precisely what contradiction, understudied group, or limitation motivates the current inquiry.",
                      "type": "definition"
                    },
                    {
                      "body": "1. Shared Ground: Clinical mentoring improves retention. 2. Gap: Yet rural clinics lack peer density. 3. Aim: This study evaluates hybrid cross-district pairing across 12 rural clinics.",
                      "type": "example",
                      "title": "Three-Step Funnel Intro"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "steps",
                      "items": [
                        "Open cleanly in the specific field rather than sweeping grand generalities (\"Throughout human history...\").",
                        "Locate the exact unresolved puzzle prior citations leave open.",
                        "Present paper structure in one crisp closing roadmap sentence."
                      ],
                      "title": "Applying Structured Abstracts & Roadmapping"
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Opening with six disconnected quotes failed to tell examiners why the topic mattered now.",
                      "type": "case_study",
                      "title": "Unmotivated Literature Dump",
                      "takeaway": "Framing the explicit methodological gap upfront clarified the contribution instantly."
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Start right inside current scholarly dialogue instead of ancient sweeping warmups.",
                      "type": "callout",
                      "title": "Ban \"Since the Dawn of Time\"",
                      "variant": "tip"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "knowledge_check",
                      "prompt": "What essential pivot distinguishes a focused academic introduction from pure background review?",
                      "options": [
                        "Defining every basic term",
                        "Explicitly naming the unresolved gap or contradiction motivating your specific inquiry",
                        "Adding extra historical footnotes"
                      ],
                      "explanation": "Identifying the scholarly gap clarifies why your paper adds fresh value.",
                      "correctIndex": 1
                    }
                  ],
                  "videos": [],
                  "summary": "Funnel framing anchors scholarly readers neatly inside active academic conversation.",
                  "position": 2,
                  "resources": [
