                      "text": "Sustaining High-Presence Habits",
                      "type": "heading",
                      "level": 2
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Make one listening commitment a visible standard: put away phones during 1:1s, check back meaning before acting on ambiguous requests, ask one extra clarifying \"What else?\" before wrapping tough calls, and invite direct feedback twice a year on how heard your teammates feel around you.",
                      "type": "paragraph"
                    },
                    {
                      "term": "The \"What Else?\" Habit",
                      "text": "Asking gently \"What else is weighing on this before we decide?\" near dialogue endings—frequently surfacing the single bold truth held back earlier.",
                      "type": "definition"
                    },
                    {
                      "body": "\"We seem aligned on launch—before we lock Friday, what else feels slightly shaky on your radar?\"",
                      "type": "example",
                      "title": "Uncovering Hidden Risks Before Close"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "steps",
                      "items": [
                        "Practice one clean listening habit weekly.",
                        "Ask \"What else?\" at key decision closes.",
                        "Check periodically with teammates whether they feel safe surfacing bad news early."
                      ],
                      "title": "Applying Daily Habits of Master Listeners"
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Asking \"What else feels shaky?\" in the final two minutes prompted a quiet QA tester to mention an unreviewed mobile checkout edge case—saving major launch bugs.",
                      "type": "case_study",
                      "title": "The Honest Launch Save",
                      "takeaway": "One thoughtful habit protects entire teams."
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Assume every colleague holds at least one valuable constraint you have not yet seen.",
