                  "id": "133d8a57-3e49-93bf-63c6-06b65c6631a6",
                  "title": "The Non-Awkward Closing Referral Question",
                  "blocks": [
                    {
                      "text": "Natural Network Branching",
                      "type": "heading",
                      "level": 2
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "At the end of an energizing chat, never pressure hosts for unposted roles. Instead ask casually: \"As I explore this path over next month, is there 1 colleague, newsletter, or local community group you'd suggest checking out—or one person worth following?\" Asking broadly for wise directions often prompts hosts spontaneously offering warm intros or flagging upcoming roles cleanly on their own.",
                      "type": "paragraph"
                    },
                    {
                      "term": "Organic Referral Prompt",
                      "text": "Inviting recommendations for communities, mentors, or next voices to learn from rather than putting hosts on an uncomfortable immediate hiring spot.",
                      "type": "definition"
                    },
                    {
                      "body": "\"Before we wrap, any thoughtful newsletter or 1–2 folks in UX research you'd recommend I read or connect with next?\"",
                      "type": "example",
                      "title": "Graceful Closing Question"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "steps",
                      "items": [
                        "Never blindside informational contacts with sudden demands for resumes pushed.",
                        "Accept suggestions warmly and credit hosts when reaching onward.",
                        "Send crisp same-day thank-you note naming 1 key takeaway."
                      ],
                      "title": "Applying The Non-Awkward Closing Referral Question"
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Three clean informational chats branching gracefully one helpful intro at a time connected an emerging analyst to a direct team hiring manager smoothly.",
                      "type": "case_study",
                      "title": "Organic Chain of Warm Intros",
                      "takeaway": "Gentle branching compounds trust organically."
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Specific thank-you notes mentioning \"your point about testing copy before styling really clicked\" prove deep real listening.",
