                    {
                      "text": "Separating Query Structure from Data Parameters",
                      "type": "heading",
                      "level": 2
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Always pass user values via bound parameters (`$1, $2` or SDK `.eq(\"slug\", value)`). Validate enum values, numeric bounds, and UUID formats at the API boundary so malformed payloads fail with crisp 400 errors rather than database crashes.",
                      "type": "paragraph"
                    },
                    {
                      "term": "Parameterized Query",
                      "text": "A database statement keeping SQL syntax strictly separate from user-supplied parameter values sent out-of-band to the engine.",
                      "type": "definition"
                    },
                    {
                      "body": "Query `.eq(\"slug\", cleanSlug)` or `where slug = $1` rather than template-interpolating `slug` into raw SQL strings.",
                      "type": "example",
                      "title": "Safe Lookup"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "steps",
                      "items": [
                        "Ban template literal SQL interpolation with request inputs.",
                        "Validate status enums against strict allowlists.",
                        "Clamp pagination limits (`Math.min(100, limit)`)."
