                      "title": "Applying Parameterized Queries & Strict Input Typing"
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Parameterizing sort/filter inputs and allowlisting sort column names eliminated arbitrary SQL clause injection permanently.",
                      "type": "case_study",
                      "title": "Injected Filter Bypass",
                      "takeaway": "Never trust dynamic column names without an allowlist map."
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Parameters protect values—never column/table names; validate dynamic sort columns against an explicit switch/Set.",
