                      "text": "Establishing Cohesive Visual Language",
                      "type": "heading",
                      "level": 2
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Art Direction governs the sensory world behind every layout: lighting direction (soft morning natural daylight vs. moody high-contrast studio shadows), color temperature (warm ochre earth tones vs. cool slate crispness), camera perspective (candid eye-level craft vs. crisp flatlay overhead), and explicit off-limits clichés (zero cheesy fake boardroom high-fives!).",
                      "type": "paragraph"
                    },
                    {
                      "term": "Art Direction Spec",
                      "text": "Explicit visual rules defining lighting, color palette grading, lens perspective, props, and authenticity standards unifying photos, illustrations, and video.",
                      "type": "definition"
                    },
                    {
                      "body": "Natural window light from side, warm neutral stone backgrounds, human hands actively building real tools, subtle matte contrast—zero isolated white-box cliparts.",
                      "type": "example",
                      "title": "Authentic Craft Art Direction"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "steps",
                      "items": [
                        "Curate 6–8 cohesive reference images sharing identical lighting and warmth before selecting stock or shooting.",
                        "Specify exact surface textures and wardrobe/prop colors harmonizing with brand palette.",
                        "Ban cheesy overly staged stock tropes explicitly inside brand guides."
                      ],
                      "title": "Applying Art Direction: Unifying Mood, Lighting & Subject"
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Replacing mixed brightly saturated stock photos with calm natural-lit documentary photos of real staff raised client perceived value immediately across an entire website.",
                      "type": "case_study",
                      "title": "Instant Brand Maturity Shift",
                      "takeaway": "Unified photography carries half the emotional weight of a brand."
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Cool icy blue photos clash visibly against warm cream-and-terracotta palettes unless graded thoughtfully.",
