                {
                  "id": "cd6177d7-df08-097c-9b0d-f1036f81f080",
                  "title": "Category Frame & Positioning Strategy",
                  "blocks": [
                    {
                      "text": "April Dunford’s Positioning Logic",
                      "type": "heading",
                      "level": 2
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Great **Positioning** deliberately frames HOW buyers evaluate you! Follow April Dunford’s proven sequence: (1) Name **True Competitive Alternatives** (`Excel, slow generalist agencies`), (2) Isolate your **Unique Capabilities** rivals lack (`48-hr standardized launch`), (3) Translate strictly into **Real Customer Value** (`ship campaigns 3 weeks earlier cleanly`), (4) Define **Exact Best-Fit Target Buyers** who care deeply right now, and (5) Choose your sharpest **Market Category** framing pricing naturally upward!",
                      "type": "paragraph"
                    },
                    {
                      "term": "Market Category Framing",
                      "text": "Intentionally anchoring a product inside a mental market category (`\"Async Video Check-Ins\"` vs `\"Generic Meeting Software\"`) so buyers instantly compare fair value instead of judging wrong price points.",
                      "type": "definition"
                    },
                    {
                      "body": "Compete as `\"General Web Design\"` -> Instantly compared against $200 marketplace templates! Reframe cleanly as `\"Conversion-Tested Checkout Architecture for Regional E-Commerce\"` -> Immediately compared cleanly against $30k revenue upside!",
                      "type": "example",
                      "title": "Reframing Away From Cheap Rivals"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "steps",
                      "items": [
                        "Write out all 5 Dunford positioning ingredients cleanly on one shared team page BEFORE writing ad copy!",
                        "Accept bravely that choosing crisp positioning explicitly means sounding less appealing to poor-fit mass buyers (`that makes ideal buyers say \"YES, built specifically for us!\"`).",
                        "Revisit positioning annually only when new buyer segments or structural market shifts warrant fresh clarity."
                      ],
                      "title": "Applying Category Frame & Positioning Strategy"
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Calling a focused team scheduling tool `\"All-in-One Business Operating System\"` forced buyers comparing it instantly against giant enterprise suites where it looked tiny and incomplete.",
                      "type": "case_study",
                      "title": "Confused Swiss-Army Positioning",
                      "takeaway": "Reframing cleanly as `\"Effortless Shift Rostering for Busy Clinics\"` skyrocketed immediate understanding and wins!"
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Weak brands try sounding attractive to everyone and compel nobody; bold positioning speaks unmistakably straight to exact right-fit customers!",
                      "type": "callout",
                      "title": "Embrace Intentional Exclusion",
                      "variant": "tip"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "knowledge_check",
                      "prompt": "Under April Dunford’s Positioning method, why clearly define exact **Competitive Alternatives** FIRST?",
                      "options": [
                        "To copy competitor homepages",
                        "Because every unique feature advantage only matters relative to what actual alternative buyers would use or do if you vanished",
                        "To calculate web hosting fees"
                      ],
                      "explanation": "True differentiation shines clearly only relative to buyers’ real realistic alternative choices (`including spreadsheets/inaction`).",
                      "correctIndex": 1
                    }
                  ],
                  "videos": [],
                  "summary": "Deliberate category framing and sharp differentiation lift offers safely out of brutal commodity price wars.",
                  "position": 2,
                  "resources": [
