                  "blocks": [
                    {
                      "text": "Balanced Personality Polarities",
                      "type": "heading",
                      "level": 2
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Give teams clear creative rails using 3–4 paired **Voice Polarities (`\"This, Not That\"`)**: e.g., **Direct, Never Cold**; **Playful, Never Goofy**; **Expert Mentor, Never Pretentious Lecturer**. Accompany each trait immediately with real copy swaps (`We write: \"Three steps to cut invoice stress\" / Never: \"Unlock paradigm invoicing synergy\"`), unifying website, product buttons, and customer apology notes effortlessly!",
                      "type": "paragraph"
                    },
                    {
                      "term": "Voice Polarity Guardrail",
                      "text": "Defining brand personality cleanly through paired contrast extremes (`Confident, NOT Arrogant`; `Warm, NOT Sloppy`), preventing uneven tone swings across teams and channels.",
                      "type": "definition"
                    },
                    {
                      "body": "Consistent tone holds even during crises: a Playful-never-Goofy brand keeps helpful microcopy light in routine setup YET shifts immediately calm, empathetic, and plain during a sensitive billing outage—never joking about lost user money!",
                      "type": "example",
                      "title": "Applying Voice Across Tough Moments"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "steps",
                      "items": [
                        "Pair every desired brand personality adjective immediately with its boundary shadow (\"Never...\").",
                        "Establish clear **Tone Adaptation Rules** explaining how voice flexes softly across celebratory launches vs. customer bug apologies.",
                        "Keep curated `\"Golden Examples\"` snippets alive showing peak brand voice in emails, tweets, and headers cleanly!"
                      ],
                      "title": "Applying Verbal Voice & \"We Are This, Never That\" Guardrails"
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "A cheeky quirky beverage brand kept automated joke error messages live (`\"Oopsie woopsie! Wallet sad?\"`) during a major double-billing payment crash, infuriating panicked shoppers.",
                      "type": "case_study",
                      "title": "Tonal Outage Disaster",
                      "takeaway": "Clarifying tone-shift boundaries across serious failure moments protects warmth without appearing callous!"
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Like an articulate friend: your core personality (`Voice`) stays yours whether giving a toast OR consoling grief (`Tone shifts compassionately to fit stakes`).",
                      "type": "callout",
                      "title": "Tone Flexes; Voice Stays Constant",
                      "variant": "tip"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "knowledge_check",
                      "prompt": "Why always define a `\"Never That\"` shadow boundary beside every brand personality adjective (`Witty, never sarcastic`)?",
                      "options": [
                        "Adds visual columns",
                        "Stops writers and designers from pushing desirable personality traits awkwardly into extreme embarrassing caricature",
                        "Replaces legal review"
