            {
              "id": "78f92834-1e8d-9170-ebcb-46ee492bf2a3",
              "title": "Module 3: Tactical Empathy, Calibrated Questions & Silence",
              "lessons": [
                {
                  "id": "667b6032-97f4-cf10-29b2-774906614bdf",
                  "title": "Tactical Empathy: Labeling & Mirroring Emotions",
                  "blocks": [
                    {
                      "text": "Disarming Tension With Calm Observation",
                      "type": "heading",
                      "level": 2
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Borrowed from Chris Voss (`Never Split the Difference`): calm **Mirroring** (`repeating the buyer’s critical 2–3 words upward gently + 4s pause: \"...way over budget?\"`) encourages them cleanly to reveal true hidden issues voluntarily! Pair with **Labeling** (`\"It sounds like your team got burned previously paying big retainers without clear ROI...\"`)—naming fears respectfully drops defensive armor almost instantaneously.",
                      "type": "paragraph"
                    },
                    {
                      "term": "Tactical Labeling",
                      "text": "Calmly naming the counterparty’s likely underlying worry or constraint neutrally (\"It seems like...\", \"It sounds like...\") inviting honest confirmation or correction without argumentative defensiveness.",
                      "type": "definition"
                    },
                    {
                      "body": "Buyer: \"Whoa, $9k is way too rich for Q3!\" Weak response: \"Let me cut to $7k!\" Tactful Label: \"Sounds like committing $9k out of Q3’s tight cash window feels risky right now—what happens inside your team if you wait until Q4 vs. trim Phase 1 scope?\"",
                      "type": "example",
                      "title": "Disarming Sticker Shock"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "steps",
                      "items": [
