                  "blocks": [
                    {
                      "text": "Strict Env Prefix Boundaries & .env Hygiene",
                      "type": "heading",
                      "level": 2
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Everything inside `dist/` is public to anyone opening View Source. Allow ONLY intentionally public endpoints and RLS-governed anon keys in `VITE_*` vars. Keep `service_role` keys, database passwords, webhook signing secrets, and third-party API secrets strictly inside server-side `process.env`—never in frontend source or Git.",
                      "type": "paragraph"
                    },
                    {
                      "term": "Public Anon Key vs Service Role Key",
                      "text": "The Supabase `anon` key is designed for browsers and strictly constrained by RLS; the `service_role` key bypasses ALL RLS and must never reach client code.",
                      "type": "definition"
                    },
                    {
                      "body": "Commit `.env.example` with empty placeholder keys (`VITE_SUPABASE_URL=`) while listing `.env` and `.env.*` inside `.gitignore`.",
                      "type": "example",
                      "title": "Fail-Safe `.env.example`"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "steps",
                      "items": [
                        "Audit `src/` and `dist/` builds for `service_role` or high-entropy secrets.",
                        "Never hardcode admin passwords or fallback credentials inside client files.",
                        "Rotate keys immediately if a secret ever enters Git history."
                      ],
                      "title": "Applying Client Bundle Exposure vs Server Secrets"
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "A developer accidentally prefixed a database admin key with `VITE_ADMIN_KEY`, exposing full database access inside main.js within minutes of deploy.",
                      "type": "case_study",
                      "title": "Bundled Admin Secret Leak",
                      "takeaway": "Prefix rules exist for immediate auditability."
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Adding `.env` to `.gitignore` does NOT remove an already-committed `.env`—rotate compromised secrets immediately!",
