                {
                  "id": "6fddcab3-627d-831e-9aa3-9f4becbe1150",
                  "title": "Decide & Commit vs. Consensus Fatigue",
                  "blocks": [
                    {
                      "text": "Reversible Speed & Disagree-and-Commit",
                      "type": "heading",
                      "level": 2
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Categorize decisions honestly: irreversible one-way doors (pricing tier structures, database security, public brand shifts) merit thorough consensus vetting; easily reversible two-way doors (button layout test, internal meeting time, pilot flyer) require swift decisive picking by the Accountable owner, trial testing, and genuine \"disagree-and-commit\" team backing afterward.",
                      "type": "paragraph"
                    },
                    {
                      "term": "Two-Way vs. One-Way Door",
