                    {
                      "text": "New teams start polite (Forming), clash as real constraints and role overlaps collide (Storming), stabilize explicit agreements (Norming), and hit high trusting velocity (Performing). Recognizing Storming as normal role calibration—never fatal team failure—lets leaders establish RACI and retro hygiene cleanly rather than panicking.",
