                    {
                      "text": "Designing Content Everyone Can Access",
                      "type": "heading",
                      "level": 2
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Accessible content strategy builds inclusion directly into briefs and editorial checklists: clean sequential headings (`H1 -> H2 -> H3` without skipping levels for styling), plain descriptive link text, structured alt descriptions on meaningful diagrams, clear transcripts/captions on audio/video derivatives, and inclusive non-exclusionary examples across cultural personas.",
                      "type": "paragraph"
                    },
                    {
                      "term": "Structural Heading Accessibility",
                      "text": "Using HTML heading levels strictly in logical semantic order (`H1 -> H2 -> H3`) so screen readers scan page architecture accurately instead of picking heading tags purely for font size.",
                      "type": "definition"
                    },
                    {
                      "body": "Broken: Jumping from `H1` straight to `H4` because `H4` looked prettier. Clean: Maintaining strict `H1 -> H2 -> H3` sequence visually styled via CSS cleanly.",
                      "type": "example",
                      "title": "Accessible vs. Broken Hierarchy"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "steps",
                      "items": [
                        "Audit links for meaningful descriptive text (\"Download Cost Worksheet\" vs. \"Read more\").",
                        "Mandate transcripts + closed captions right inside video/podcast brief scopes.",
                        "Verify readable high-contrast typography and plain-language reading comfort universally."
                      ],
                      "title": "Applying Accessibility & Inclusive Content Governance"
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "A brilliant flagship product series omitted closed captions and readable transcripts, locking out hearing-impaired buyers and non-native audio listeners simultaneously.",
                      "type": "case_study",
                      "title": "Inaccessible Video Tutorial Launch",
                      "takeaway": "Adding accurate clean transcripts boosted comprehension and search discovery overnight."
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "If an image illustrates conceptual process (`Pillar-Spoke hub`), summarize that meaning clearly; skip verbose alt clutter on purely decorative swirls (`alt=\"\"`).",
