                      "text": "Structured Conversion Hypotheses",
                      "type": "heading",
                      "level": 2
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Smart copy iteration tests high-leverage elements first—hero value proposition, pricing framing, or objection-handling—using clean hypotheses grounded in research: \"Changing headline from [generic feature] to [VoC outcome] will boost signup clicks because visitor feedback showed confusion about use case.\" Measure meaningful downstream actions, never vanity clicks alone.",
                      "type": "paragraph"
                    },
                    {
                      "term": "Copy Test Hypothesis",
                      "text": "A clear testable statement linking a specific copy change, expected user impact metric, and research-backed behavioral reason.",
                      "type": "definition"
                    },
                    {
                      "body": "\"Swapping hero subhead to explicitly confirm zero coding setup will lift trial starts because exit polls flagged technical intimidation among solo owners.\"",
                      "type": "example",
                      "title": "Clean Hero Copy Hypothesis"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "steps",
                      "items": [
                        "Test large structural shifts (offer clarity, proof placement) before tiny punctuation tweaks.",
                        "Anchor every hypothesis in real support chats, heatmaps, or VoC insights.",
                        "Evaluate down-funnel quality (activated accounts), not pure click curiosity."
                      ],
                      "title": "Applying Hypothesis-Led Copy Optimization"
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Testing a sensationalist ad headline raised clicks 80%—while tanking actual demo bookings 50% because leads felt misled.",
                      "type": "case_study",
                      "title": "Misleading Clickbait Test",
                      "takeaway": "Always pair top-of-funnel click tracking with real conversion rate downstream."
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Small sites lack traffic to split-test button shades reliably; test bold messaging clarity upgrades instead.",
                      "type": "callout",
                      "title": "Prioritize Big Messaging Bets",
                      "variant": "tip"
                    },
