                  "id": "b31d2cd8-ae5b-e46e-77f2-d189b3e02894",
                  "title": "Why Over-Engineered CRMs Die Quickly",
                  "blocks": [
                    {
                      "text": "Minimum Viable CRM Design",
                      "type": "heading",
                      "level": 2
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "A CRM serves TWO simple jobs: **remembering clean context reliably across people** and **surfacing timely follow-ups nobody drops**. Keep data structures ruthlessly lean: separate **Contacts** (`individual humans`), **Accounts** (`organizations/households`), and **Deals/Lifecycles** (`time-bounded pipelines`). Restrict mandatory properties strictly to fields genuinely driving routing, reporting, or renewal dates—auto-capturing emails/timestamps passively wherever software allows.",
                      "type": "paragraph"
                    },
                    {
                      "term": "CRM Bloat Failure",
                      "text": "Loading customer databases with dozens of rarely read mandatory custom fields causing staff frustration, garbage placeholder entries, and quiet reversion to messy personal spreadsheets.",
                      "type": "definition"
                    },
                    {
                      "body": "Instead of 20 forced checkboxes at lead entry, mandate strictly `Email/Name + Source + Primary Goal + Next Action Date`. Capture deep billing or compliance fields cleanly ONLY when deals advance toward Proposals!",
                      "type": "example",
                      "title": "Clean Minimal Stage Gate"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "steps",
                      "items": [
                        "Cut unused legacy custom properties nobody touched inside 90 days.",
                        "Require strictly an explicit **Next Action Date** on every open active account/deal—zero dateless floating cards!",
                        "Enforce consistent naming conventions (`Acme Corp — Q4 Onboarding`) preventing duplicate lookalikes cleanly."
                      ],
                      "title": "Applying Why Over-Engineered CRMs Die Quickly"
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "A 12-person agency invested thousands configuring an elaborate 60-field enterprise CRM—within six weeks reps kept real honest notes inside private personal Google Sheets!",
                      "type": "case_study",
                      "title": "The Ghost Spreadsheet Rebellion",
                      "takeaway": "Stripping CRM forms down strictly to 5 helpful fields restored 100% enthusiastic adoption within ten days!"
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "An active CRM item lacking a specific scheduled follow-up date is functionally dead—enforce clean next-date views weekly!",
                      "type": "callout",
                      "title": "Every Active Deal Demands a Future Date",
                      "variant": "tip"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "knowledge_check",
                      "prompt": "Why do over-customized CRM setups with 25+ required input fields routinely fail in real teams?",
                      "options": [
