                      "text": "Structure experience bullets cleanly: **Strong Action Verb + What You Built/Owned + Context/Tools + Measurable Result or Quality Improvement**. Quantify where honest (time saved, error drop, team size, completion rate) without inventing fake percentages—even qualitative operational proof (\"Standardized 12 onboarding templates used across 4 cohorts\") beats vague adjectives.",
                      "type": "paragraph"
                    },
                    {
                      "term": "Impact Bullet",
                      "text": "A resume line proving tangible contribution (\"Reduced weekly reporting prep from 4 hrs to 45 mins by building a clean spreadsheet template\") rather than listing generic duties.",
                      "type": "definition"
                    },
                    {
                      "body": "Weak: \"Helped with customer emails.\" Strong: \"Resolved 35+ weekly billing and onboarding tickets within a 4-hour SLA while drafting 6 reusable FAQ replies.\"",
                      "type": "example",
                      "title": "Before vs After Rewrite"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "steps",
                      "items": [
                        "Replace passive phrases (\"Responsible for\", \"Assisted with\") with direct verbs.",
                        "Tailor top 2–3 summary lines and skill order directly to target role needs.",
                        "Lead with strongest, most relevant projects—even if unpaid or capstone work."
                      ],
                      "title": "Applying Achievements Over Duties: The Impact Formula"
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Rewriting a fresh grad’s resume from duties to concrete course & volunteer deliverables lifted interview callbacks from 0/20 to 4/12 cleanly.",
                      "type": "case_study",
                      "title": "Zero-Callback Turnaround",
                      "takeaway": "Proof of execution beats generic buzzwords."
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Never fabricate fake \"% revenue lifts\"—concrete scope (\"built 8-page accessible site\", \"audited 25 listings\") reads far more credibly.",
                      "type": "callout",
                      "title": "Honest Clarity Beats Fake Numbers",
                      "variant": "tip"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "knowledge_check",
                      "prompt": "What separates a strong CV bullet from a weak job description line?",
                      "options": [
                        "Using larger decorative fonts",
                        "Showing specific action, context/tools, and concrete outcome rather than passive duties",
                        "Listing every hobby"
                      ],
                      "explanation": "Concrete actions and verifiable results help hiring managers picture your impact fast.",
                      "correctIndex": 1
