                  "id": "022e77ae-c93e-94fa-20f9-405bb41897ad",
                  "title": "Building Lightweight Project Style Sheets",
                  "blocks": [
                    {
                      "text": "Single-Page Style Governance",
                      "type": "heading",
                      "level": 2
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Whenever editing articles over 1,000 words or multi-author hubs, keep one compact living **Style Sheet** logging exact choices once: spelling locale (`US` vs. `UK`), serial Oxford comma policy, number rules (`spell one–nine, numerals 10+`, `%` vs. `percent`), heading capitalization (`Title Case` vs. `Sentence case`), and domain vocabulary (`Log in` verb vs. `login` noun). Consistency signals world-class craft instantly.",
                      "type": "paragraph"
                    },
                    {
                      "term": "Editorial Style Sheet",
                      "text": "A concise shared reference capturing per-project capitalization, punctuation, spelling variants, number formatting, and bespoke term conventions for 100% document uniformity.",
                      "type": "definition"
                    },
                    {
                      "body": "Locale: US English | Serial Comma: Yes | Headings: Sentence case | Percent: `%` numeral (`8%`, never `eight percent`) | Auth terms: `sign in` (verb), `sign-in` (adjective).",
                      "type": "example",
                      "title": "Mini Style Entry"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "steps",
                      "items": [
                        "Record tough brand/spelling decisions cleanly the first moment they appear in Edit Pass 1.",
                        "Reference a consistent core authority (AP, Chicago, or house standard) rather than inventing ad-hoc whims.",
                        "Run focused Search checks (`Ctrl+F`) per tricky term across entire documents (`website` vs `web site`, `%` vs `percent`)."
                      ],
                      "title": "Applying Building Lightweight Project Style Sheets"
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "An international report toggled erratically between `colour`/`color`, `12 percent`/`12%`, and `E-commerce`/`ecommerce` across sections.",
                      "type": "case_study",
                      "title": "Mixed Dialect & Casing Mess",
                      "takeaway": "Applying one quick 12-item style sheet synchronized every page in 25 minutes cleanly."
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Keep clear distinctions cleanly: `log in` / `set up` / `follow up` (two words as verbs) vs. `login` / `setup` / `follow-up` (one word or hyphenated as nouns/adjectives).",
                      "type": "callout",
                      "title": "Verb vs. Noun Compound Forms",
                      "variant": "tip"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "knowledge_check",
                      "prompt": "Why maintain a bespoke project Style Sheet alongside standard grammar dictionaries?",
                      "options": [
                        "Dictionaries omit verbs",
                        "Standard rules allow multiple equally valid variants (`12%` vs `12 percent`)—your style sheet locks one consistent choice per project",
                        "Replaces topic sentences"
                      ],
                      "explanation": "Uniform convention choices eliminate erratic internal visual friction completely.",
                      "correctIndex": 1
                    }
