                        "A well-known strategy built on short-term wins",
                        "A strategy that is well-known-now"
                      ],
                      "explanation": "Pre-noun compounds hyphenate (`well-known`, `short-term`), while `-ly` adverbs never take hyphens.",
                      "correctIndex": 1
