                  "blocks": [
                    {
                      "text": "Respectful Suggesting & Constructive Queries",
                      "type": "heading",
                      "level": 2
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "When marking drafts in Suggesting/Track Changes, toggle markup cleanly so routine mechanical fixes don’t obscure critical structural notes—or handle clean mechanical fixes smoothly with clear changelog overview while highlighting interpretive unknowns via concise **Author Queries (`[AQ]`)**. Never ask blunt condescending queries (`\"What does this even mean??\"`); ask helpfully (`\"[AQ: Confirm whether Q3 churn figure reflects gross or net retention so Table 2 matches text?]\"`).",
                      "type": "paragraph"
                    },
                    {
                      "term": "Author Query (AQ)",
                      "text": "A concise, neutral, constructive marginal comment asking the original writer to clarify ambiguous facts, supply missing citations, or approve sensitive phrasing shifts.",
                      "type": "definition"
                    },
                    {
                      "body": "Harsh: \"Makes zero sense—rewrite!\" Constructive: \"[AQ: By 'fast turnaround', can we state an exact SLA here (e.g., within 24 hours) so enterprise readers see concrete commitment?]\"",
                      "type": "example",
                      "title": "Helpful vs. Harsh Query"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "steps",
                      "items": [
                        "Pair concrete specific questions inside AQs with an easy suggested option when appropriate.",
                        "Avoid lecturing authors in exclamation-heavy margins—keep tone partner-like and supportive.",
                        "Deliver clean Accept-Ready copies alongside tracked diffs when appropriate for fast client sign-off."
                      ],
                      "title": "Applying Clean Markup Hygiene & Author Queries"
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Returning a heavily restructured 2,000-word manuscript purely as chaotic overlapping cross-outs left a founder too overwhelmed to approve changes.",
                      "type": "case_study",
                      "title": "Drowning in Tracked Edits",
                      "takeaway": "Sending a clean polished final version PLUS highlighted summary key queries got approved in one afternoon cleanly."
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "After major flow edits, share a clean readable copy alongside your marked version so writers experience smooth final flow effortlessly.",
                      "type": "callout",
                      "title": "Deliver Both Clean & Tracked When Restructuring Heavily",
                      "variant": "tip"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "knowledge_check",
                      "prompt": "What defines a constructive, collaborative Author Query inside edited drafts?",
                      "options": [
