                {
                  "id": "de411a4c-dbf5-2cb6-c513-57d27820e3b5",
                  "title": "Non-Defensive Feedback With SBI",
                  "blocks": [
                    {
                      "text": "Situation-Behavior-Impact Feedback Loop",
                      "type": "heading",
                      "level": 2
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "The Situation-Behavior-Impact (SBI) model anchors feedback in observable moments rather than personality labels. Naming when and where something happened (Situation), exactly what was said or done (Behavior), and its measurable effect on users or teammates (Impact) turns vague tension into solvable adjustments.",
                      "type": "paragraph"
                    },
                    {
                      "term": "SBI Model",
                      "text": "Feedback framework sequencing Situation (time/place), Behavior (observable action), and Impact (concrete consequence) followed by collaborative dialogue.",
                      "type": "definition"
                    },
                    {
                      "body": "\"In yesterday's client demo (S), when feature pricing was introduced before confirming pain points (B), the buyer raised budget objections before seeing value (I). How did that flow feel from your seat?\"",
                      "type": "example",
                      "title": "Using SBI With a Peer"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "steps",
                      "items": [
                        "Wait until emotions cool enough for constructive focus.",
                        "Stick strictly to observable behaviors—never mind-read motives.",
                        "Ask for their perspective before prescribing fixes."
                      ],
                      "title": "Applying Non-Defensive Feedback With SBI"
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Telling an analyst they \"need to be more proactive\" created anxiety with zero clue what daily habit to change.",
                      "type": "case_study",
                      "title": "Vague Criticism Failure",
                      "takeaway": "Replacing trait labels with concrete SBI examples produced immediate improvement next sprint."
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Absolute words trigger instant defensiveness; ground every observation in one specific recent event.",
                      "type": "callout",
                      "title": "Avoid \"Always\" & \"Never\"",
                      "variant": "tip"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "knowledge_check",
                      "prompt": "Which statement follows the Situation-Behavior-Impact structure correctly?",
                      "options": [
                        "You never listen in sprint reviews.",
                        "During Tuesday planning (S), interrupting twice while Maya walked through QA risks (B) meant two edge cases were skipped (I).",
                        "You are a careless communicator during meetings."
                      ],
                      "explanation": "SBI cites specific time/place, observable behavior, and tangible impact without personal labels.",
                      "correctIndex": 1
                    }
                  ],
