                  "completion_criteria": "Study the core frameworks in \"Warm Boundaries & Saying No Cleanly\", verify the inline knowledge check, and apply the practical checklist."
                },
                {
                  "id": "1d55bfed-b7ce-76e0-a7ef-1b8dc07a1a71",
                  "title": "De-Escalating Frustrated Threads",
                  "blocks": [
                    {
                      "text": "Pause, Validate, Clarify, Solve",
                      "type": "heading",
                      "level": 2
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Never hit send inside five minutes of reading an aggravating email—draft offline, sleep or take a 20-minute walk, and strip every defensive barb out. Open by neutrally validating the sender’s core concern (\"I hear how disruptive Tuesday’s invoice delay was for your month-end close\"), own facts transparently, present concrete next steps, or move hot disagreements straight onto a calm 10-minute call.",
                      "type": "paragraph"
                    },
                    {
                      "term": "20-Minute Cooling Draft",
                      "text": "Writing a response into empty blank notes—never inside the live Reply box with recipient addresses filled—and reviewing calmly after cooling off.",
                      "type": "definition"
                    },
                    {
                      "body": "\"Thanks for flagging the duplicate billing right away, Maya. I’ve voided Invoice #882 this morning and confirmed credit reflects within 48 hours. Happy to jump on a quick call at 2 PM if helpful.\"",
                      "type": "example",
                      "title": "De-Escalating Tense Reply"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "steps",
                      "items": [
