                    {
                      "text": "Psychologists distinguish high emotional granularity—pinpointing subtle shades like disappointed, sidelined, overloaded, or uncertain—as core to composure. Naming accurately directs exact action: uncertainty calls for clarifying specs, whereas feeling sidelined calls for a candid role chat.",
