                      "text": "Emotional reasoning treats intense feelings as proof of external truth (\"I feel inadequate, so they think I failed\"). Pausing to separate camera facts (\"The director requested 2 revised ROI slides\") from dramatic mind stories lowers stress rapidly and guides focused editing.",
                      "type": "paragraph"
                    },
                    {
                      "term": "Cognitive Reframe",
                      "text": "Evaluating stressed automatic thoughts against verifiable facts to adopt accurate, proportionate, constructive perspectives.",
