                    {
                      "text": "When a proposal fails, fixed thinking blames permanent talent (\"I'm just awful at pitches\"). Constructive attribution isolates changeable factors: did discovery miss a real budget owner, or did evidence arrive late? Adjusting strategy rather than sulking builds rapid mastery and calm confidence.",
