                    },
                    {
                      "text": "When customers actively patch spreadsheets together, hire manual temp help, or spend frustrating hours solving an issue today, budget urgency already exists. Selling \"vitamins\" (mildly nice improvements nobody searches for) forces expensive persuasion; solving painful bottlenecks sells through natural relief.",
