                      "text": "Measured Experiment Learning Gates",
                      "type": "heading",
                      "level": 2
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Separate core **Mission Vision** (who you help) cleanly from **Strategy Hypotheses** (pricing model, channel, product shape). When honest 4–6 week sprints miss clear pre-set traction thresholds despite multiple messaging tweaks, audit carefully: do buyers love parts of the solution while rejecting the wrapper (`Zoom-In Pivot`), or want the same workflow tailored to an adjacent buyer (`Customer Segment Pivot`)? Pivot deliberately off observed pull—never random panic.",
                      "type": "paragraph"
                    },
                    {
                      "term": "Zoom-In Pivot",
                      "text": "Turning what originally existed as one modest secondary feature inside a broader startup into the entire sharp central flagship product because customers genuinely pulled that single piece relentlessly.",
                      "type": "definition"
                    },
                    {
                      "body": "Early startup built an all-in-one fitness studio platform; users ignored 80% of tools while loving the automated SMS class-waitlist filler -> Pivoted cleanly onto dedicated Waitlist Automation and grew rapidly.",
                      "type": "example",
                      "title": "Real Evidence-Led Pivot"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "steps",
                      "items": [
                        "Set calm 60-day evaluation checkpoints anchored on actual paid retention—not vanity page clicks.",
                        "Look carefully for unexpected pockets where specific customers show intense delight (`\"Where did usage surprise us?\"`).",
                        "Make one focused variable change per pivot cycle rather than scrambling brand, buyer, AND product blindly at once!"
                      ],
                      "title": "Applying When to Pivot vs. Persevere With Evidence"
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Switching startup domains completely every three weeks prevented any single message from gaining market awareness.",
