                {
                  "id": "f3df93b5-7487-a910-6e58-de413a0cc88b",
                  "title": "Reading the Balance Sheet Snapshot Intuitively",
                  "blocks": [
                    {
                      "text": "Assets, Liabilities & Working Capital",
                      "type": "heading",
                      "level": 2
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Every Balance Sheet locks in strict harmony: **Assets (`What we own: Cash, Receivables, Inventory, Gear`) = Liabilities (`What we owe: Vendor Bills, Payroll Due, Debt`) + Equity (`Owner capital + Retained cumulative profits`)**. Watching **Current Ratio (`Current Assets / Current Liabilities`)** confirms instantly whether short-term cash & receivables comfortably cover bills due within 12 months (`healthy >= 1.5x`).",
                      "type": "paragraph"
                    },
                    {
                      "term": "Working Capital",
                      "text": "Short-term operating cushion (`Current Assets minus Current Liabilities`) showing net accessible liquid buffer powering day-to-day inventory, payroll, and bill cycles cleanly.",
                      "type": "definition"
                    },
                    {
                      "body": "Checking: $45k Cash + $25k Receivables (`$70k Current Assets`) vs. $30k Vendor Bills + $10k Short Tax Due (`$40k Current Liabilities`) -> Healthy `1.75x` Current Ratio!",
                      "type": "example",
                      "title": "Quick Liquidity Check"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "steps",
                      "items": [
                        "Check Current Assets vs Current Liabilities monthly—don’t trap everything in slow illiquid gear!",
                        "Monitor Debt-to-Equity gently so loan interest never chokes operating flexibility during slow quarters.",
                        "Watch sudden bloating in Inventory or Uncollected Receivables quietly masking cash strain."
                      ],
                      "title": "Applying Reading the Balance Sheet Snapshot Intuitively"
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Tied 100% of surplus profits into specialized warehouse machinery leaving $3,000 cash against $28,000 short bills due next Tuesday—forcing high-interest emergency credit lines.",
                      "type": "case_study",
                      "title": "Illiquid Asset Trap",
                      "takeaway": "Holding sensible liquid reserves protects operations effortlessly against brief timing dips!"
                    },
