                      "text": "Justifying Every Dollar Freshly",
                      "type": "heading",
                      "level": 2
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Borrow **Zero-Based Budgeting (`ZBB`)** principles annually (or across top 10 expense lines quarterly): require major expense categories to justify fresh return cleanly from `$0` baseline (`\"If we started clean tomorrow, would we genuinely sign this $1,800/mo analytics contract again?\"`). Auditing software seats, unused vendor retainers, and duplicated agencies routinely frees 10–18% pure clean net margin silently!",
                      "type": "paragraph"
                    },
                    {
                      "term": "Zero-Based Review",
                      "text": "Evaluating ongoing budgets from a clean `$0` justification baseline—requiring each recurring expense to re-prove current strategic ROI rather than automatically inheriting last year’s allocations.",
                      "type": "definition"
                    },
                    {
                      "body": "Checking literal bank/card statements reveals 7 zombie SaaS seats (`$460/mo = $5,520/yr`) lingering cleanly from departed hires and paused trials—cancelled immediately!",
                      "type": "example",
                      "title": "Quarterly Subscription Sweep"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "steps",
                      "items": [
                        "Audit actual credit-card and ACH vendor feeds line-by-line every 90 days.",
                        "Require business owners to attach a clear purpose + owner name directly on every recurring tool over $50/mo.",
                        "Distinguish mandatory compliance/delivery spend cleanly from nice-to-have discretionary experiments."
                      ],
                      "title": "Applying Zero-Based Rigor Over Lazy \"+5% Everywhere\" Budgets"
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "A 20-person company paid simultaneously for three overlapping project apps, two PDF tools, and unused CRM licenses wasting $14,000 yearly quietly.",
