                {
                  "id": "a402d1db-4416-a3c1-3b21-e8a1f7dd3274",
                  "title": "Handling Scope Creep & Tough Feedback Gracefully",
                  "blocks": [
                    {
                      "text": "The \"Yes, And Here Are Two Options\" Pivot",
                      "type": "heading",
                      "level": 2
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Welcome extra ideas warmly—then anchor cleanly inside agreed scope: \"Love that blog filter idea! Since our current milestone focuses on the core shop launch, we can either: **Option A** add it as a small Phase-2 sprint next week for £280, or **Option B** swap out the FAQ block to keep the budget identical. Which fits your priority better?\"",
                      "type": "paragraph"
                    },
                    {
                      "term": "Scope Creep",
                      "text": "The gradual, unpriced expansion of agreed project deliverables through \"just one quick extra\" requests mid-project.",
                      "type": "definition"
                    },
                    {
                      "body": "Giving the client control between a paid add-on or swapping an equivalent scoped item removes all friction while preserving your rate.",
                      "type": "example",
                      "title": "Graceful Scope Pivot"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "steps",
                      "items": [
                        "Validate client goals before discussing scope boundaries.",
                        "Present two clear commercial/trade-off options calmly.",
                        "Document approved change orders in writing before starting extra tasks."
                      ],
                      "title": "Applying Handling Scope Creep & Tough Feedback Gracefully"
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Offering a calm Phase-2 option on three extra requests led a satisfied client to sign a steady £600/mo ongoing improvement retainer.",
                      "type": "case_study",
                      "title": "Turned Freebie Into Retainer",
                      "takeaway": "Professional boundaries attract better budgets."
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Sometimes a messy client request (\"make the logo 3x bigger!\") hides a simple clarity worry (\"I worry visitors miss our brand\") solvable cleanly.",
