                    {
                      "id": "fe11-1",
                      "text": "From URL to Rendered Page",
                      "type": "heading"
                    },
                    {
                      "id": "fe11-2",
                      "text": "When a visitor types a URL, the browser resolves the domain name via DNS, opens a secure HTTPS connection, and requests the HTML document. As the HTML streams in, the browser builds the Document Object Model (DOM), fetches linked stylesheets to build the CSS Object Model (CSSOM), combines them into a Render Tree, calculates box geometry (Layout), and paints pixels to the screen.",
                      "type": "paragraph"
                    },
                    {
                      "id": "fe11-3",
                      "rows": [
                        [
                          "HTML",
                          "Semantic meaning and document outline",
                          "Choose elements by meaning (<nav>, <article>), not appearance"
                        ],
                        [
                          "CSS",
                          "Visual typography, colour, spacing, and layout",
                          "Keep styling decoupled from markup using classes and variables"
                        ],
                        [
                          "JavaScript",
                          "Dynamic state, events, validation, and data fetching",
                          "Progressively enhance semantic markup rather than breaking native links"
                        ]
                      ],
                      "type": "table",
                      "title": "The Three Core Frontend Layers",
                      "headers": [
                        "Layer",
                        "Responsibility",
                        "Best Practice"
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "id": "fe11-4",
                      "type": "knowledge_check",
                      "prompt": "Which two internal trees does the browser combine before computing element positions on screen?",
                      "options": [
                        "DNS Tree and File Tree",
                        "DOM and CSSOM",
                        "JSON Tree and Event Loop"
                      ],
                      "explanation": "The browser merges the parsed HTML (DOM) and parsed styles (CSSOM) into the Render Tree prior to Layout and Paint.",
                      "correctIndex": 1
                    }
