                  "id": "6db49de5-2409-2dfd-35b6-7674f8591b7f",
                  "title": "The Four Forces of Customer Switching",
                  "blocks": [
                    {
                      "text": "Push, Pull, Anxiety & Habit Inertia",
                      "type": "heading",
                      "level": 2
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Every switch battles four forces cleanly: **Push of Present Pain** (broken export crashes right ahead of client presentation!) + **Pull of New Solution** (appealing promise of clean 5-minute fixes) must overpower **Anxiety of New Risk** (\"What if migrating data breaks everything?\") + **Habit of Current Routine** (\"At least we know where old folders sit\"). Lowering Anxiety (`easy guided import + free trial`) unlocks switches far cheaper than shouting louder features!",
                      "type": "paragraph"
                    },
                    {
                      "term": "Four Switching Forces",
                      "text": "Behavioral balance between active catalysts driving change (`Push of Current Pain + Pull of New Hope`) against friction holding buyers still (`Anxiety of Transition + Familiar Habit`).",
                      "type": "definition"
                    },
                    {
                      "body": "Instead of doubling discount coupons (`Push/Pull`), an accounting switch launched `\"Free 24-Hour White-Glove Historical Data Migration\"` directly crushing switching **Anxiety**—doubling migrations effortlessly!",
                      "type": "example",
                      "title": "Switching Barrier Rescue"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "steps",
                      "items": [
                        "Audit recent switched buyers asking literally `\"What specific frustration day finally made you look around?\"` (`Trigger Event`).",
                        "Identify top 2 transition anxieties (`learning curve, team pushback, lost history`).",
                        "Build dedicated onboarding bridges dismantling those exact anxieties rather than solely shouting product hype!"
                      ],
                      "title": "Applying The Four Forces of Customer Switching"
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Dropping monthly software price 30% barely moved hesitant buyers who didn’t fear $15—they feared losing five years of organized PDF archives during migration!",
                      "type": "case_study",
                      "title": "Discounting Wrong Friction",
                      "takeaway": "Offering 1-click lossless archive imports sparked switches at FULL list price cleanly!"
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Eliminating transition risk converts wary buyers reliably at healthy full margins!",
                      "type": "callout",
                      "title": "Lower Anxiety Over Raising Discounts",
                      "variant": "tip"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "knowledge_check",
                      "prompt": "Why did a free 24-hour data import guarantee double customer signups better than a 30% discount?",
                      "options": [
                        "Users dislike cheaper prices",
                        "Directly crushed Switching Anxiety (\"fear of messy migration loss\") which actually blocked action more than small price tags",
                        "Discounts hurt search speed"
                      ],
                      "explanation": "Pinpointing exact friction forces (`Anxiety vs Habit`) beats blind price cutting every time.",
                      "correctIndex": 1
                    }
