              "lessons": [
                {
                  "id": "6d199c35-95fd-43a5-d43c-3162d311e543",
                  "title": "Bottom-Up Market Sizing vs. Lazy \"1% of Billions\"",
                  "blocks": [
                    {
                      "text": "Counting Real Addressable Customers",
                      "type": "heading",
                      "level": 2
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Credible **TAM** (`Total Addressable Market`), **SAM** (`Serviceable Available Market` matching language, compliance, price fit), and **SOM** (`Serviceable Obtainable Market` realistically reachable over 24–36 months) build strictly **Bottom-Up**: `Verified Count of Target Customers (e.g., 42,000 independent dental clinics via public directories) x Realistic Annual Price You Actually Charge ($1,800/yr) = $75.6M SAM`. Bottom-up clarity proves you literally know WHO buys and WHERE they live!",
                      "type": "paragraph"
                    },
                    {
                      "term": "Bottom-Up Market Sizing",
                      "text": "Calculating realistic market revenue ceilings by multiplying verified counts of narrow target buyers/accounts directly by realistic achievable average annual contract pricing—rather than top-down analyst report slices.",
                      "type": "definition"
                    },
                    {
                      "body": "Target: US Independent Physical Therapy Clinics (~19,000 licensed practices per national association data) x Realistic Annual Software Plan ($1,440/yr) = **$27.4M SAM** (Regional Beachhead Year-2 SOM targeting 250 clinics = $360k ARR cleanly achievable!).",
                      "type": "example",
                      "title": "Crisp Bottom-Up Walk-Through"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "steps",
                      "items": [
                        "Verify target organization/buyer counts via reliable public sources (`bls.gov`, government business registries, trade associations).",
                        "Multiply strictly by YOUR realistic annual contract pricing—not inflated competitor bundles!",
                        "Show narrow Year-1–2 SOM clearly tied to literal sales/marketing reach math!"
                      ],
                      "title": "Applying Bottom-Up Market Sizing vs. Lazy \"1% of Billions\""
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Using an arbitrary $150B \"Global Healthcare\" press figure masked that the startup’s niche tool only fit tiny 3-person outpatient optometrists totaling $18M globally.",
                      "type": "case_study",
                      "title": "Diluted Billion-Dollar Illusion",
                      "takeaway": "Honest bottom-up sizing guided smart conservative capital planning right from Day 1 cleanly."
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Free third-party summary sites routinely invent inflated billions—always inspect primary labor/census counts directly!",
                      "type": "callout",
                      "title": "Watch Multi-Report Double Counting",
                      "variant": "tip"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "knowledge_check",
                      "prompt": "Why do experienced executives reject Top-Down `\"Just 1% of a $50B Market\"` sizing immediately?",
                      "options": [
                        "Math seems too small",
                        "Confuses unrelated mega-industries with actual reachable buyer counts and hides zero real understanding of unit distribution",
                        "Percentages look blurry"
                      ],
                      "explanation": "Bottom-up unit counts verify genuine buyer density and realistic revenue ceilings transparently.",
                      "correctIndex": 1
                    }
                  ],
                  "videos": [],
                  "summary": "Bottom-up counts anchor strategic ambition inside hard verifiable demographic truth.",
                  "position": 1,
