                    {
                      "text": "Always compute `Gross-Margin LTV = (Average Order Value x Repeat Purchases or Avg Lifespan) x Gross Margin %`, and `CAC = (Media Spend + Creative/Agency/Promo Costs) / New Acquired Customers`. Healthy scalable businesses generally target `LTV:CAC >= 3:1` and recover CAC cash within realistic Payback windows matching available working capital.",
                      "type": "paragraph"
                    },
                    {
                      "term": "Gross-Margin LTV",
                      "text": "Total expected gross profit (Revenue minus COGS/delivery/payment costs) generated over a customer’s realistic lifetime—never raw top-line sales alone.",
                      "type": "definition"
                    },
                    {
                      "body": "Order = £100, COGS+Ship = £55 -> Gross Profit = £45. Paying £50 CPA loses cash Day 1 unless repeat retention within 90 days recovers it cleanly!",
                      "type": "example",
                      "title": "Cash Trap Math"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "steps",
                      "items": [
                        "Include fulfillment, discounts, and refunds inside gross margin calculations.",
                        "Track Paid CAC separately from Blended CAC (which includes organic lifts).",
                        "Verify actual 60-day/90-day cohort retention rather than assuming hopeful 5-year lifespans."
                      ],
                      "title": "Applying Margin-Adjusted LTV & Payback Windows"
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "A subscription box chased 2.1x Day-1 revenue ROAS that actually lost £14 cash per customer after fulfillment costs and Month-2 churn—raising order bundling and tightening CPA saved cash flow cleanly.",
                      "type": "case_study",
                      "title": "Rescuing a \"High-ROAS\" Cash Crunch",
                      "takeaway": "Profit math rules real strategy."
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Recovering CAC inside 60–90 days lets lean teams reinvest cash safely without debt strain.",
