                {
                  "id": "c9464d07-8c3b-10fe-d6c1-9f6b2c52852c",
                  "title": "Presenting 3-Option MESO Offers",
                  "blocks": [
                    {
                      "text": "Multiple Equivalent Simultaneous Offers (MESOs)",
                      "type": "heading",
                      "level": 2
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Presenting three thoughtfully balanced options—differing in scope depth, timeline, and fee structure—signals flexibility without dropping your standards. Seeing how a partner chooses among Option A, B, or C reveals their true priorities instantaneously while shifting the question from \"Yes or No?\" to \"Which fit works best?\"",
                      "type": "paragraph"
                    },
                    {
                      "term": "MESO Strategy",
                      "text": "Offering two or three equally acceptable package configurations simultaneously so partner choices uncover true priorities safely.",
                      "type": "definition"
                    },
                    {
                      "body": "Tier 1: Core audit (£3.5k, 2 wks) | Tier 2: Audit + 3-month sprint (£8.5k, net-15) | Tier 3: Full retained partnership (£4k/mo x 6mo).",
                      "type": "example",
                      "title": "Three-Tier Agency Options"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "steps",
                      "items": [
                        "Build 3 tiers that all satisfy your baseline margin.",
                        "Highlight differences cleanly across 4 clear rows.",
                        "Ask \"Which option aligns closest to your Q3 targets?\""
                      ],
                      "title": "Applying Presenting 3-Option MESO Offers"
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "A web studio replaced single-price PDFs with 3-tier scoped packages; clients stopped demanding blanket discounts and mostly chose Tier 2.",
                      "type": "case_study",
                      "title": "Doubled Proposal Win Rate",
                      "takeaway": "Choice architecture turns haggling into collaborative selection."
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Showing the comprehensive premium option sets natural quality framing cleanly.",
                      "type": "callout",
                      "title": "Anchor With Top Tier First",
                      "variant": "tip"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "knowledge_check",
                      "prompt": "What psychological benefit do Multiple Equivalent Simultaneous Offers provide?",
                      "options": [
                        "They confuse buyers with complex tax rules",
                        "They reveal buyer priorities safely while protecting your acceptable profit levels",
                        "They reduce contract duration automatically"
                      ],
                      "explanation": "Choosing between acceptable packages shows what buyers value most.",
                      "correctIndex": 1
                    }
                  ],
                  "videos": [],
                  "summary": "Structured option packages guide partners toward confident selection.",
                  "position": 2,
                  "resources": [
                    {
