                      "text": "Bottom-Line Framing for Busy Colleagues",
                      "type": "heading",
                      "level": 2
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Academic essays build suspense toward a conclusion; professional documents state the verdict upfront. Giving busy decision-makers the problem, recommendation, resource cost, and decision date in the top block respects their calendar while positioning supporting detail cleanly below.",
                      "type": "paragraph"
                    },
                    {
                      "term": "Decision Memo",
                      "text": "A concise internal document presenting context, 2–3 evaluated options, a clear recommendation, and a requested sign-off deadline.",
                      "type": "definition"
