                      "text": "Balanced Option Comparison",
                      "type": "heading",
                      "level": 2
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "When proposing resource commitments, briefly compare two or three viable alternatives—including doing nothing or choosing a phased rollout—across cost, speed, and risk. Explaining fairly why alternatives fall short proves you did thorough analysis and makes your recommendation stronger.",
                      "type": "paragraph"
                    },
                    {
                      "term": "Option Matrix",
                      "text": "A compact side-by-side table comparing competing paths across cost, timeline, effort, and downside risk.",
                      "type": "definition"
                    },
                    {
                      "body": "Compare Option A (Manual Patch: $0, high ongoing labor), Option B (Staged SaaS Tool: $300/mo, 2-week rollout - Recommended), and Option C (Custom Build: 12 weeks).",
                      "type": "example",
                      "title": "Three-Option Budget Frame"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "steps",
                      "items": [
                        "Include the baseline status-quo option honestly.",
                        "Select 3–4 consistent criteria (cost, speed, risk, quality).",
                        "Declare your recommended pick cleanly beneath the comparison."
