              "id": "32dfcc3a-076c-b0d1-ac10-780f84b9b832",
              "title": "Module 1: Charters, Scope Boundaries & Explicit Non-Goals",
              "lessons": [
                {
                  "id": "1464ec88-fcaf-4f45-5366-7cba2419accf",
                  "title": "Why Vague Kickoffs Trigger Late Scope Creep",
                  "blocks": [
                    {
                      "text": "Charter Alignment & Explicit Non-Goals",
                      "type": "heading",
                      "level": 2
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Every dependable project opens with a tight **1-Page Project Charter** locking five anchors BEFORE build hours spend: (1) **Objective / Done Definition**, (2) **Key Deliverables**, (3) **Single DRI Owner (`Directly Responsible Individual`)**, (4) **Time/Budget Guardrails**, and most powerfully (5) **Explicit Out-of-Scope / Non-Goals**—listing tempting side requests specifically deferred outside Phase 1!",
                      "type": "paragraph"
                    },
                    {
                      "term": "Explicit Non-Goals",
                      "text": "Documenting specific attractive ideas, features, or edge cases intentionally excluded from the current project boundary up front so later additions require calm scope trade-offs rather than silent overwork.",
                      "type": "definition"
                    },
                    {
                      "body": "Goal: Launch clean Q3 mobile invoice view. Out-of-Scope (Phase 1 Non-Goals): Multi-currency export conversion, custom theme builders, and legacy archive migrations (`slated Q4`).",
                      "type": "example",
                      "title": "Powerful Non-Goals Line"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "steps",
                      "items": [
                        "Draft the 1-page charter in 30 minutes BEFORE task-board tickets ever get created.",
                        "Review Non-Goals aloud directly with the sponsor until both agree cleanly in writing.",
                        "Assign literally ONE primary DRI name per outcome—never \"Team Marketing\" as shared owner!"
                      ],
                      "title": "Applying Why Vague Kickoffs Trigger Late Scope Creep"
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Two teams built incompatible landing flows over five weeks because nobody signed a crisp Non-Goals clause stating interactive calculators waited for Phase 2.",
                      "type": "case_study",
                      "title": "Silent Rework Collapse",
                      "takeaway": "One shared 5-line Non-Goals box slashed rework completely on subsequent launches!"
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "When two people co-own a critical milestone equally, both silently assume the other checked the handoff—assign ONE DRI clearly!",
                      "type": "callout",
                      "title": "One Owner Per Deliverable",
                      "variant": "tip"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "knowledge_check",
                      "prompt": "Why add an explicit \"Out-of-Scope / Non-Goals\" section inside a concise Project Charter?",
                      "options": [
                        "To pad document page count",
                        "Prevents conflicting hidden assumptions across stakeholders and establishes fair trade-off boundaries against late scope creep",
                        "Eliminates user research"
                      ],
                      "explanation": "Naming what you are NOT building now protects budget, schedule, and team clarity up front.",
                      "correctIndex": 1
                    }
                  ],
                  "videos": [],
                  "summary": "Clear charters turn blurry wishes into accountable shared execution agreements.",
