                      "text": "Pattern Grouping & Impact Ranking",
                      "type": "heading",
                      "level": 2
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "After collecting observations, group raw symptoms under 3–5 overarching diagnostic themes—and rank them by business or user severity rather than alphabetical order. Addressing one root bottleneck often clears six downstream symptoms simultaneously.",
                      "type": "paragraph"
                    },
                    {
                      "term": "Root-Cause Clustering",
                      "text": "Grouping scattered operational defects under shared systemic drivers (e.g., training gaps, unclear handoffs, missing validation) before prioritizing fixes.",
                      "type": "definition"
                    },
                    {
                      "body": "Instead of 8 scattered bugs, group Finding 2.0 as \"Missing Pre-Send Validation\" unifying duplicate emails, wrong totals, and truncated names.",
