                  "title": "Open Loops & Middle Retention Resets",
                  "blocks": [
                    {
                      "text": "Bridging Sections Forward",
                      "type": "heading",
                      "level": 2
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Never cleanly close a subtopic and pause vaguely before starting the next (\"Okay, that’s Step 1. Now Step 2 is...\"). Bridge cleanly using forward tension (\"Now that fixes speed—yet if you miss this next permission setting, backups still fail silently\") paired with gentle visual shifts—reframed angles, music subtle resets, or fresh demo tabs.",
                      "type": "paragraph"
                    },
                    {
                      "term": "Section Bridge Loop",
                      "text": "Transitioning seamlessly out of a completed explanation by surfacing the exact next bottleneck or question before pause fatigue sets in.",
                      "type": "definition"
                    },
                    {
                      "body": "\"Fixing subject lines gets emails opened—though one common mistake inside paragraph two still kills 70% of replies. Look right here:\"",
