                {
                  "id": "e82059b5-f48a-ce8a-8f00-acab3e920094",
                  "title": "Preventing Keyword Cannibalization",
                  "blocks": [
                    {
                      "text": "Intent Differentiation & Merge Strategy",
                      "type": "heading",
                      "level": 2
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Keyword cannibalization strikes when two pages on your site pursue virtually the same reader question (`\"how to write cold emails\"` vs `\"cold email writing guide\"`), splitting links, confused click signals, and rankings. Either separate intent cleanly (one strictly **Beginner Tutorial** vs. one strictly **Downloadable Templates Gallery**) OR merge both thoroughly into one powerhouse master page with a clean redirect.",
                      "type": "paragraph"
                    },
                    {
                      "term": "Keyword Cannibalization",
                      "text": "Having multiple overlapping pages on the same domain competing against one another for identical search intent, fragmenting authority and causing fluctuating rankings.",
                      "type": "definition"
                    },
                    {
                      "body": "If two posts both explain general B2B invoice etiquette, merge into one master guide. Only keep separate URLs when intent genuinely splits (`\"Invoice Etiquette Guide\"` vs. `\"Free PDF Invoice Generator Tool\"`).",
                      "type": "example",
                      "title": "Intent Split vs. Merge"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "steps",
                      "items": [
                        "Search your own site (`site:yourdomain.com \"topic\"`) before greenlighting new briefs to verify you haven’t covered that exact intent already.",
                        "Diagnose fluctuating URL swaps in search performance logs.",
                        "Merge weak duplicates into the stronger historical URL and redirect permanently (`301`)."
                      ],
                      "title": "Applying Preventing Keyword Cannibalization"
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "A growing blog wrote \"CRM Guide 2024\", \"What Is a CRM?\", and \"Choosing a CRM System\" separately with overlapping paragraphs; all three stalled on Page 2.",
                      "type": "case_study",
                      "title": "Self-Inflicted Ranking Split",
                      "takeaway": "Merging overlapping intro theory and clearly differentiating tool comparison pushed the unified master guide straight onto Page 1."
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Running `site:yoursite.com [topic]` takes five seconds inside any content brief and eliminates accidental cannibalization completely.",
                      "type": "callout",
                      "title": "Search Your Own Domain First",
                      "variant": "tip"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "knowledge_check",
                      "prompt": "When is keeping two closely related topic URLs justified instead of merging them?",
                      "options": [
                        "When both explain identical beginner theory in different adjectives",
                        "When each page clearly serves a distinct search intent (e.g., an educational guide vs. a free downloadable template/tool)",
                        "When written by different interns"
                      ],
                      "explanation": "Distinct user intents deserve distinct tailored experiences; identical intents belong unified.",
                      "correctIndex": 1
                    }
                  ],
                  "videos": [],
                  "summary": "Clean URL intent boundaries eliminate self-competition and focus organic authority.",
                  "position": 2,
                  "resources": [
                    {
                      "id": "da17bcb2-4e7c-4728-b46f-5d6659225436",
