                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Michael Gerber’s classic observation stands true everywhere: when quality exists strictly inside the owner’s head, every sick day or surge breaks customer promises. Systematization does NOT mean cold rigid corporate manuals—it means crisp 1-page checklists, pre-staged starter bins, and clear standard routines letting ordinary trained staff deliver remarkable consistency calmly!",
                      "type": "paragraph"
