                    {
                      "text": "Searching Before Scaling",
                      "type": "heading",
                      "level": 2
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "As Steve Blank defined cleanly, a startup isn’t a smaller version of a large company—it is a nimble temporary organization built to **search for a repeatable, scalable business model**. Until paying strangers repeatedly stick around (`Product-Market Fit`), speed of honest customer learning outweighs slick perfection everywhere.",
                      "type": "paragraph"
                    },
                    {
                      "term": "Search vs. Execution Mode",
                      "text": "Operating lightly with rapid experiments to discover proven customer pull (`Search`) before locking heavy fixed overhead, hiring sales armies, or automating (`Execution`).",
                      "type": "definition"
                    },
                    {
                      "body": "Spending 4 months designing elaborate referral programs, custom logos, and scalable microservice clusters before verifying 10 people finish week-one onboarding.",
                      "type": "example",
                      "title": "Premature Execution Trap"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "steps",
                      "items": [
                        "Write down your riskiest assumption on Value (Will users care?) and Growth (How do we reach them affordably?).",
                        "Refuse heavy scaling investments until core retention stabilizes cleanly.",
                        "Optimize every weekly sprint strictly for learning speed over vanity polish."
                      ],
                      "title": "Applying A Startup Is a Temporary Search Organization"
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Two founders burned half their initial seed check on leased space and conference hoodies before shipping a test build to ten real buyers.",
                      "type": "case_study",
                      "title": "Premature Logo & Office Splurge",
                      "takeaway": "Keeping burn tiny preserves double runway to discover true traction calmly."
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Assume 70% of your brilliant Day-1 guesses carry subtle flaws—your job is finding out cheaply this month instead of next year!",
