                    {
                      "text": "Borrow real scientific discipline: formulate tests explicitly beforehand: `\"We believe [Exact Persona] experiences [Pain]; if we offer [Minimum Experience], at least [Concrete Threshold, e.g. 4 of 20] will [Measurable Costly Action: pay $20 / submit workflow] within [7 days].\"` Pre-committing thresholds stops founders from moving goalposts after quiet results!",
                      "type": "paragraph"
                    },
                    {
                      "term": "Minimum Success Criterion",
                      "text": "The smallest concrete numeric outcome agreed strictly BEFORE launching an experiment that warrants investing another sprint into that hypothesis.",
                      "type": "definition"
                    },
                    {
                      "body": "Belief: Freelance bookkeepers dread chasing missing bank CSVs. Test: Offer automated reminder link to 25 bookkeepers. Success Threshold: >= 6 configure active client reminders within 10 days.",
