            {
              "id": "2277fca9-1a50-e391-f8c9-018da7b9b77f",
              "title": "Module 3: Metrics That Matter, Retention & PMF Signals",
              "lessons": [
                {
                  "id": "8ac6ed65-bf79-f00f-ce0a-ab2caf38e8d8",
                  "title": "Why Retention Beats Acquisition Every Time",
                  "blocks": [
                    {
                      "text": "Cohort Retention & Flattening Curves",
                      "type": "heading",
                      "level": 2
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Split signups cleanly by joining month/week (**Cohorts**) and track what percentage STILL actively gain core value in Weeks 2, 4, 8, and 12. If every single cohort curves relentlessly down toward 0%, **you do NOT have Product-Market Fit—pause ads immediately!** Real PMF appears visually when retention curves stop dropping and flatten cleanly (`e.g., leveling steadily around 25–40%` long-term active repeat usage).",
                      "type": "paragraph"
                    },
                    {
                      "term": "Leaky Bucket Trap",
                      "text": "Growing gross total user signups rapidly through paid ads or PR spikes while hidden monthly cohorts churn continuously toward 0% repeat usage.",
                      "type": "definition"
                    },
                    {
                      "body": "Startup A: 10,000 signups/mo, Day-30 active = 1% (failing core value!). Startup B: 300 signups/mo, Day-30 active = 42% flat steadily across 6 months (authentic PMF seed ready to grow!).",
                      "type": "example",
                      "title": "Diagnosing Flattening Retention"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "steps",
                      "items": [
                        "Never aggregate total cumulative signups (\"50,000 lifetime users!\")—track Weekly/Monthly Active Cohorts strictly!",
                        "Interview 10 churned users gently (\"Where did it fall flat in Week 1?\") alongside 10 power-retainers.",
                        "Measure frequency matching real problem pace (daily chat vs. monthly tax close!)."
                      ],
                      "title": "Applying Why Retention Beats Acquisition Every Time"
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Landing on national tech podcasts brought 15,000 curious clicks in one weekend—by Week 4 only 40 active accounts remained because onboarding stalled.",
                      "type": "case_study",
                      "title": "PR Spike Mirage",
                      "takeaway": "Fixing Week-1 activation workflows ahead of broad PR turns modest launches into compounding engines cleanly."
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Ask active testers cleanly: `\"How disappointed would you feel if this product vanished tomorrow? (Very / Somewhat / Not)\"`—exceeding ~40% \"Very Disappointed\" strongly marks early PMF!",
                      "type": "callout",
                      "title": "Ask the Sean Ellis 40% Question",
                      "variant": "tip"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "knowledge_check",
                      "prompt": "What visual pattern on a Cohort Retention Chart confirms authentic emerging Product-Market Fit?",
                      "options": [
                        "Total cumulative signups rising upward forever",
                        "Cohort active percentages dropping initially then flattening horizontally into a steady repeating floor above zero",
                        "90% bounce inside 10 seconds"
                      ],
                      "explanation": "A flattening curve proves a real core segment extracts indispensable recurring value cleanly.",
                      "correctIndex": 1
                    }
                  ],
                  "videos": [],
                  "summary": "Cohort clarity keeps founders ruthlessly honest about whether users genuinely love and keep the product.",
                  "position": 1,
                  "resources": [
