                      "text": "Curating Indexed Real Moments",
                      "type": "heading",
                      "level": 2
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Great speakers rarely invent brilliant stories on stage; they maintain living notebooks capturing small surprising moments, customer frustrations, and personal lessons week by week. Tagging 8–10 tested stories by theme (`Trust`, `Failure`, `Speed`, `Conflict`) equips you for any room instantly.",
                      "type": "paragraph"
                    },
                    {
                      "term": "Story Bank",
                      "text": "A maintained personal index recording brief true narratives tagged by theme, audience fit, length, and key turning point.",
                      "type": "definition"
                    },
                    {
                      "body": "Tag: Scope Creep / Boundaries | Hook: The $400 Friday Redesign | 60-word Spine + Core Takeaway.",
                      "type": "example",
                      "title": "Sample Bank Entry"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "steps",
                      "items": [
                        "Jot down interesting moments weekly before details evaporate.",
                        "Tag entries by strategic lesson rather than just calendar date.",
                        "Test new stories in low-stakes peer conversations before keynotes."
                      ],
                      "title": "Applying Building Your Reusable Story Bank"
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Smart engineers froze when asked \"Tell me about a time a launch went sideways\" because wins and fixes blurred together.",
                      "type": "case_study",
                      "title": "Blank Interview Syndrome",
                      "takeaway": "Keeping a 6-item indexed story sheet made interview delivery natural and poised."
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "When someone says something wonderfully human or surprising, write the exact phrase into notes before lunch ends.",
