              "lessons": [
                {
                  "id": "e96bc221-1ce3-5c8f-aa62-a10e039e64f4",
                  "title": "Why \"Grow 40% & Improve Quality\" Isn’t Strategy",
                  "blocks": [
                    {
                      "text": "Richard Rumelt’s Strategy Kernel",
                      "type": "heading",
                      "level": 2
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Great strategy follows three crisp elements (`The Strategy Kernel`): (1) **Honest Diagnosis** (`identifying the single biggest root obstacle or opportunity genuinely driving outcomes`), (2) **Guiding Policy** (`overall strategic approach concentrating force around that constraint`), and (3) **Coherent Actions** (`mutually reinforcing moves aligned cleanly under that policy`). Without diagnosing the real bottleneck first, tactics scatter blindly everywhere!",
                      "type": "paragraph"
                    },
                    {
                      "term": "Strategy Kernel",
                      "text": "Three-part discipline uniting (1) clear Diagnosis of the core challenge, (2) focused Guiding Policy choosing an explicit path, and (3) Coherent reinforcing Actions working together instead of pulling apart.",
                      "type": "definition"
                    },
                    {
                      "body": "Fluff: \"We will delight all users with AI excellence and scale revenue.\" Kernel: \"Diagnosis: SMB buyers quit Week 1 over setup complexity. Policy: Win strictly on 15-minute zero-code setup for solo clinics (`refusing custom enterprise bloat`). Actions: Cut 8 complex settings, ship 6 clinic presets, price flat $49/mo.\"",
                      "type": "example",
                      "title": "Fluff vs. Strategy Kernel"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "steps",
                      "items": [
                        "Name the ONE brutal bottleneck truthfully before brainstorming tactics.",
                        "Audit current weekly team work: delete busy projects actively working AGAINST your chosen Guiding Policy!",
                        "Demand clear logic explaining WHY your chosen actions unlock multiplied force together."
                      ],
                      "title": "Applying Why \"Grow 40% & Improve Quality\" Isn’t Strategy"
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "A regional software team spread six engineers thinly across enterprise compliance, consumer mobile apps, AND developer APIs simultaneously—losing cleanly to three focused specialists.",
                      "type": "case_study",
                      "title": "Peanut-Butter Strategy Failure",
                      "takeaway": "Concentrating all 6 engineers strictly onto clinic workflows captured market leadership inside 14 months!"
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Strategy isn’t doing everything nicely—it’s piling asymmetric focused force cleanly onto one decisive lever!",
                      "type": "callout",
                      "title": "Concentration Beats Spread",
                      "variant": "tip"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "knowledge_check",
                      "prompt": "What separates genuine Strategic Guiding Policy from motivating corporate goal slogans (\"Grow Revenue 50%\")?",
                      "options": [
                        "Longer slide fonts",
                        "Goals state desired destination outcomes; Strategy diagnoses the core structural hurdle and picks coherent concentrated choices overcoming it",
                        "Goals skip numbers"
                      ],
                      "explanation": "Naming what drives results—and concentrating reinforcing moves onto it—turns ambition into real traction.",
                      "correctIndex": 1
                    }
                  ],
                  "videos": [],
                  "summary": "Clear honest diagnosis and concentrated force replace scattered busyness cleanly.",
