                  "title": "Steelmanning Opposing Views",
                  "blocks": [
                    {
                      "text": "Upgrading Opposing Logic Fairly",
                      "type": "heading",
                      "level": 2
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Steelmanning means articulating an opposing position in its sharpest, fairest, most intelligent form—often clearer than opponents expressed it—before evaluating trade-offs. If your plan survives contact with the strongest honest counterargument, your confidence rests on solid rock rather than selective echo chambers.",
                      "type": "paragraph"
                    },
                    {
                      "term": "Steelman Principle",
                      "text": "Constructing the strongest, most charitable version of an alternative view to test your own reasoning rigorously before deciding.",
                      "type": "definition"
                    },
                    {
                      "body": "Articulate: \"Waiting two extra weeks preserves brand reliability for enterprise buyers whose annual trust takes months to rebuild after glitches.\"",
                      "type": "example",
                      "title": "Steelmanning Caution on Fast Launch"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "steps",
                      "items": [
                        "Listen intently to sharpest valid concerns.",
                        "Confirm opponents agree your summary reflects their best case.",
                        "Adapt or combine strengths cleanly rather than clinging to dogma."
                      ],
                      "title": "Applying Steelmanning Opposing Views"
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Opening an executive pitch by presenting the strongest valid argument against your own path stunned critics—because nobody could surprise the presenter with unweighed counters.",
                      "type": "case_study",
                      "title": "Bulletproof Strategy Presentation",
                      "takeaway": "Pre-integrating the strongest counter creates unshakeable rigor."
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Ask \"Where is my toughest critic probably 30% right?\"—mine that gold calmly.",
                      "type": "callout",
                      "title": "Win Truth, Not Points",
