                    {
                      "text": "Gather your team before committing final sign-off and say: \"Imagine we sit here six months from now and this launch collapsed completely. Take four silent minutes and write every concrete reason why it failed.\" Shifting into prospective hindsight grants permission to voice quiet doubts safely—surfacing preventable blind spots immediately.",
                      "type": "paragraph"
                    },
                    {
                      "term": "Pre-Mortem",
                      "text": "Simulating a future failure upfront so teams surface unseen operational, adoption, or risk threats cleanly while cheap fixes remain possible.",
                      "type": "definition"
