                      "text": "Transparent Criteria Weighting",
                      "type": "heading",
                      "level": 2
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "When weighing big alternatives, lock explicit criteria weights upfront summing to 100% (e.g., User Impact 40%, Reliability 30%, Cost 20%, Speed 10%), score options honestly on verifiable benchmarks, and inspect outcomes. If scores surprise your gut, examine whether hidden emotional bias misled gut OR an uncaptured criterion belongs in the model.",
                      "type": "paragraph"
                    },
                    {
                      "term": "Weighted Criteria Matrix",
                      "text": "Structured decision grid scoring competing options transparently against pre-weighted business and user priorities totaling 100%.",
                      "type": "definition"
                    },
                    {
                      "body": "Scoring Custom Build vs. SaaS Tool across 6-month cost, security audit speed, and team maintenance burden surfaces clear objective winner fast.",
                      "type": "example",
                      "title": "Comparing Build vs. Buy Cleanly"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "steps",
                      "items": [
                        "Lock weights BEFORE scoring vendors to prevent post-hoc rigging.",
                        "Use factual scores backed by short notes.",
                        "Check sensitivity: does swapping weights slightly flip outcome completely?"
                      ],
                      "title": "Applying Weighted Multi-Criteria Decision Grids"
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Weighted scoring resolved a two-month deadlock between engineering and marketing over analytics tools inside one crisp afternoon review.",
