                      "text": "Predictable Reference Schemas",
                      "type": "heading",
                      "level": 2
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Every endpoint doc follows strict uniformity: HTTP Method + Path, clear 1-sentence summary, Authentication scope, Path/Query/Body parameter tables (`Name`, `Type`, `Required`, `Constraints`, `Description`), Sample Request, and annotated `200/201` plus `400/401/404` responses.",
                      "type": "paragraph"
                    },
                    {
                      "term": "Type & Constraint Explicitness",
                      "text": "Documenting exact data types, enum values, min/max bounds, and nullability per parameter rather than generic descriptions like \"date string\".",
                      "type": "definition"
                    },
                    {
                      "body": "`due_date` (`string`, required) — ISO-8601 date (`YYYY-MM-DD`, UTC); must fall after `issued_date`.",
                      "type": "example",
                      "title": "Unambiguous Parameter Spec"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "steps",
                      "items": [
                        "Specify required vs. optional clearly alongside sensible defaults.",
                        "Document enums explicitly (`pending`, `paid`, `void`) rather than leaving strings open.",
                        "List concrete realistic error payloads so client parsers handle failure gracefully."
                      ],
                      "title": "Applying Anatomy of an Endpoint Reference"
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Docs listed `\"created_at: timestamp\"` without stating seconds vs. milliseconds; mobile engineers sent seconds and set customer orders back to 1970.",
                      "type": "case_study",
                      "title": "Mysterious Timestamp Bug",
                      "takeaway": "Specifying `integer (Unix epoch seconds)` eliminated integration bugs cleanly."
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Realistic examples (`\"customer_email\": \"ops@northwind-bakery.example\"`) communicate domain expectations far better than meaningless placeholders.",
                      "type": "callout",
                      "title": "Ban \"foo\", \"bar\", and \"test123\"",
                      "variant": "tip"
