                    {
                      "text": "Copy-Paste Verified Snippets",
                      "type": "heading",
                      "level": 2
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Good developer docs give self-contained runnable `curl` and language SDK snippets demonstrating exact authentication headers (`Authorization: Bearer $API_KEY`), required `Content-Type` headers, and minimal valid payloads. Explaining token scopes and rate-limit headers cleanly upfront saves hours of guesswork.",
                      "type": "paragraph"
                    },
                    {
                      "term": "Minimal Runnable Example",
                      "text": "The smallest syntactically complete request developers can execute right from their terminal after supplying only their test API key.",
                      "type": "definition"
                    },
                    {
                      "body": "Include `-X POST`, URL, `-H \"Authorization: Bearer $KORD_TOKEN\"`, `-H \"Content-Type: application/json\"`, and valid minimal `-d` JSON body cleanly indented.",
