                  "title": "Changelogs & Deprecation Migration Guides",
                  "blocks": [
                    {
                      "text": "Action-Led Release & Deprecation Notices",
                      "type": "heading",
                      "level": 2
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Useful release notes categorize changes transparently (`Breaking`, `Added`, `Changed`, `Fixed`, `Deprecated`) and tell users immediately whether action is required on their end. Deprecation guides must state sunset dates clearly alongside exact old-vs-new code side-by-side.",
                      "type": "paragraph"
                    },
                    {
                      "term": "Deprecation Runway",
                      "text": "Announcing retirement of an API field or workflow early alongside exact sunset timeline and 1:1 migration mapping before removal occurs.",
                      "type": "definition"
                    },
                    {
                      "body": "Deprecated: `GET /users?role=admin` (retires Dec 31, 2026). Replace with `GET /members?filter[role]=admin`. Action needed only if polling `/users` directly.",
                      "type": "example",
                      "title": "Clear Migration Note"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "steps",
                      "items": [
                        "Place breaking changes and required actions at the absolute top.",
                        "Pair old deprecated syntax side-by-side with exact updated replacement.",
                        "Summarize end-user benefit concisely—never paste raw cryptic Git commit hashes unmodified."
                      ],
                      "title": "Applying Changelogs & Deprecation Migration Guides"
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Renaming a webhook payload key under \"Internal Cleanup\" broke dozens of merchant integrations Monday morning.",
                      "type": "case_study",
                      "title": "Silent Breaking Change Backlash",
                      "takeaway": "Publishing bright Breaking banners with exact JSON diffs restored integration goodwill fast."
                    },
                    {
