                  "blocks": [
                    {
                      "text": "Constraint-Driven Ideation & Crazy-8s",
                      "type": "heading",
                      "level": 2
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Setting sharp limits (\"Must work one-handed on a 375px screen for a busy nurse in 20 seconds\") frees creative energy cleanly. Running rapid 8-minute Crazy-8 sketching sprints forces pushing past familiar cliché shapes #1 and #2 straight toward novel layout ideas #6–#8.",
                      "type": "paragraph"
                    },
                    {
                      "term": "Crazy-8s Sprint",
                      "text": "Folding a sheet into 8 panels and sketching 8 distinct interface/concept solutions in 8 fast minutes to break fixation on your first idea.",
                      "type": "definition"
                    },
                    {
                      "body": "Removing fancy hover animations forced designing crystal-clear direct labels and instant visual status indicators working cleanly on touchscreens.",
                      "type": "example",
                      "title": "Constraint Shift"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "steps",
                      "items": [
                        "Write your user constraint and primary task explicitly at the top of the page.",
                        "Sketch 6–8 rough boxes quickly in pen without erasing.",
                        "Combine the clearest navigation from sketch #3 with the focal clarity from sketch #7."
                      ],
                      "title": "Applying Why Creative Constraints Spark Stronger Ideas"
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Replacing a cluttered 4-sidebar admin table with one clear card-queue sketched in panel #6 halved coordinator onboarding time cleanly.",
                      "type": "case_study",
                      "title": "Escaping Generic Dashboard Clones",
                      "takeaway": "Fast rough exploration protects teams from falling in love with weak first drafts."
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Pixels feel precious; messy pen boxes encourage bold experimentation cleanly without attachment.",
                      "type": "callout",
                      "title": "Sketch Ugly on Paper First",
                      "variant": "tip"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "knowledge_check",
                      "prompt": "Why do senior designers push through 6–8 rough sketches before opening Figma or code?",
