                  "blocks": [
                    {
                      "text": "Adapting Everyday Affordances Cleanly",
                      "type": "heading",
                      "level": 2
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Use SCAMPER (Substitute, Combine, Adapt, Modify, Put to another use, Eliminate, Reverse) thoughtfully: can you **Eliminate** a separate settings page? **Adapt** airport boarding-pass hierarchy onto an event ticket screen? **Reverse** long signup forms by letting visitors preview real value first?",
                      "type": "paragraph"
                    },
                    {
                      "term": "Visual Affordance",
                      "text": "Design cues (contrast, elevation, clear labels, spacing) visually signaling how an element behaves without instructions.",
                      "type": "definition"
                    },
                    {
                      "body": "Instead of trapping visitors on a 6-step registration wall first, let them try building one sample project interactively—then prompt saving progress cleanly.",
                      "type": "example",
                      "title": "Reverse Onboarding Flow"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "steps",
                      "items": [
                        "Audit existing user flows for redundant confirmation screens you can Eliminate safely.",
                        "Study how physical objects (boarding passes, pharmacy labels, metro maps) prioritize urgent clarity.",
                        "Test one unconventional rearrangement lightly with peers."
                      ],
                      "title": "Applying SCAMPER & Lateral Pattern Borrowing"
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Applying bold time-window + gate/venue hierarchy from physical boarding passes turned a confusing event PDF into an effortless instant scan.",
                      "type": "case_study",
                      "title": "Boarding Pass Ticket Redesign",
                      "takeaway": "Cross-domain patterns create instant clarity."
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Innovate on workflow clarity—never invent weird mysterious icons for standard things like Back, Search, or Save.",
