                  "blocks": [
                    {
                      "text": "Protecting Debate While Stopping Personal Attacks",
                      "type": "heading",
                      "level": 2
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Task conflict—disagreeing about launch sequence, UX clarity, or pricing tiers—improves decisions when mutual trust stays intact. Relationship conflict—assuming bad character, sarcasm, or turf sabotage—paralyzes execution. Your job as a mediator is redirecting personal hostility back onto observable operational options.",
